type: software
title: "Sign-State Algebra (⊖, ⊕, ⊗): A Visual Reformulation and Dual-Basis Computational Architecture for Commutative Tessarines"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-26
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Jasnoor Singh
    given-names: Jasnoor Singh 
repository-code: "https://github.com/singhcodez/sign-state-algebra"
url: "https://singhcodez.github.io/sign-state-algebra/"
abstract: >-
  Sign-State Algebra is a visual and computational reformulation of commutative
  tessarines (bicomplex numbers) that encodes squaring rules directly into
  geometric glyphs (⊖² = -1, ⊕² = +1, ⊗² = -1) for mathematical writing and
  collision-free ASCII suffixes (1m, 1p, 1mp) for programming. Expressions
  compile in O(1) additions into the orthogonal idempotent split basis
  e1 = (1 + ⊕)/2, e2 = (1 - ⊕)/2, halving scalar multiplications and resolving
  light-cone zero divisors via channel-restricted pseudoinverses.
keywords:
  - tessarines
  - bicomplex-numbers
  - hypercomplex-algebra
  - split-complex
  - sign-state-algebra
  - digital-signal-processing
  - mathematics-education
